        "width": 2574
      },
      {
        "alt_text": "JS Crossword\na crossword where the clue = eval(answer)\n\nWelcome to JS Crossword! Every clue is a JS eval of its answer - for example, 7 could be solved with 3+4 and [object Object] could be solved with []+{}. This crossword uses some lesser-known and cursed JS features, so I'd recommend it for people already somewhat familiar with JavaScript.\n\nYou're allowed to use the following characters: A-Za-z0-9!\"()*+-./<=>[]`{}. This means that no spaces (empty squares), commas, or semicolons are allowed to be used. The crossword is case-sensitive. The final answer consists only of english words, so it must match A-Za-z.\n\nYour answers will be evaluated within an eval() sandbox, you can try it out at the playground below. You're of course also allowed to use other resources, such as DevTools, MDN, searching etc. This crossword is human-made, so if you solve it with AI you're lame, learn to have fun.\n\nYou can change the writing direction by clicking a square or pressing ctrl. Your progress is saved",
        "height": 387,
        "media_key": "3_2058689351203127296",
        "public_metrics": {},
        "type": "photo",
        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJHvDrlXgAAg_9M.png",
        "width": 875
      },
      {
        "alt_text": "banner image - JS Crossword, a crossword where the clue = eval(answer)\n\na mini-crossword is pictured underneath as a visual example",
